RESEARCH_BRIEF.md

# Research datasets and generated model artifacts
Backend/research/datasets/raw/*
Backend/research/datasets/processed/*
Backend/research/models/*
!Backend/research/datasets/raw/.gitkeep
!Backend/research/datasets/processed/.gitkeep
!Backend/research/models/.gitkeep

# Feedback analytics training assets
training/feedback_analytics/datasets/raw/*
training/feedback_analytics/datasets/processed/*
training/feedback_analytics/models/*
!training/feedback_analytics/datasets/raw/.gitkeep
!training/feedback_analytics/datasets/processed/.gitkeep
!training/feedback_analytics/models/.gitkeep
# The scikit-learn models ship with the repo - 20MB in total, and without them a
# fresh clone has no predictions and no sentiment fallback. The fine-tuned
# DistilBERT stays ignored: model.safetensors is 255MB, over GitHub's 100MB
# per-file limit, so it is shared out of band and the code falls back to
# sentiment_model.joblib when it is absent.
!training/feedback_analytics/models/*.joblib

